{"name":"Kitty Whiskers","hex":"#b7b5b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kitty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat; a kitten.","A young cat; a kitten."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of jack (“a small, typically white, ball used as the target ball in bowls”).","A pool of money to which card players contribute a portion of their winnings, which is used for paying shared expenses such as the cost of the premises or refreshments;  any pool of money to which people contribute for shared expenses or other joint purposes; also, any fund of liquid assets set aside for future use.\n\nSynonym of pot (“a quantity of money available to be won in a round or a game”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitty"},{"term":"whiskers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of whisker","Faded creases around the crotch of blue jeans. Can be added artificially or created by daily wear over the lifetime of a garment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whiskers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kitty (2016 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Kitty is a 2016 American short fantasy-drama film directed and written by Chloë Sevigny, based on the short story of same name by Paul Bowles. The film stars Ione Skye, Lee Meriwether, and Edie Yvonne. It was screened in the Critics' Week section at the 2016 Cannes Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8a/Kitty_%28short_film_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitty_(2016_film)","wikidata":"Q22078050"},{"title":"Whiskers","blocks":[{"text":"Whiskers, also known as vibrissae, are specialized sensory hairs that help most species of mammals sense their environment. Whiskers function as highly sensitive feelers that help mammals navigate the world in many different ways, including the detection of air currents and physical objects to aid in navigation, hunting, and spatial awareness. Whiskers can trigger reflexes to protect the eyes. Whiskers also play a significant role in the communication between individual animals in different species of mammals. They convey an animal's emotional state, essentially sending a message to other members of their species about what emotion they are feeling at the time. Whisker movement can be thought of as a form of language that animals use to silently communicate with the other animals around them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Cat_whiskers_closeup.jpg/330px-Cat_whiskers_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whiskers","wikidata":"Q913572"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Chinchilla-Patchouli.jpg/500px-Chinchilla-Patchouli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Chinchilla-Patchouli.jpg/500px-Chinchilla-Patchouli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chinchilla with large macrovibrissae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChinchilla-Patchouli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg/500px-Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg/1280px-Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg/500px-Pseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Patagonian fox showing four major cranial groups of vibrissae: supraorbital (above the eye), mystacial (where a moustache would be), genal (on the cheek, far left), and mandibular (pointing down, under the snout)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APseudalopex_culpaeus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Rat_whiskers_2.jpg/500px-Rat_whiskers_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Rat_whiskers_2.jpg/1280px-Rat_whiskers_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Rat_whiskers_2.jpg/500px-Rat_whiskers_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pet rat clearly showing the grid-like arrangement of the macrovibrissae on the face, and the microvibrissae under the nostrils. The supraorbital vibrissae above the right eye are also visible.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARat_whiskers_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Hpim0279.jpg/500px-Hpim0279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Hpim0279.jpg/1280px-Hpim0279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Hpim0279.jpg/500px-Hpim0279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"All the hairs of the manatee may be vibrissae.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHpim0279.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/500px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/1280px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/500px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Macrovibrissae and supraorbital vibrissae of the common harbor seal (Phoca vitulina)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeehund.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Catyawn.jpg/500px-Catyawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Catyawn.jpg/500px-Catyawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A yawning cat shows how the mystacial macrovibrissae can be swept forward.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatyawn.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/500px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/1280px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/500px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The upper, smooth whisker belongs to a California sea lion. The lower undulated whisker belongs to a harbor seal.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg/500px-Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg/1280px-Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg/500px-Aethia_pygmaea3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_